WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.100
- For the first time ever,
first year associates

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.620
at New York law firms, that
is people who just graduated

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:08.215
from law school, are going
to start out with a salary

00:00:08.215 --> 00:00:09.950
of $200,000 or more.

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:10.970
Here's how this works.

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:13.160
There are some fancy
law firms in New York.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:15.650
It used to be Cravath, now
it tends to be Milbank Tweed

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:18.780
that set the salary that lots
of other law firms follow,

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:20.500
and this time for the first year ever,

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:24.840
Milbank Tweed is offering
first-year associates $200,000

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.390
plus bonus.

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:29.170
Fifth year associates
are gonna make $300,000,

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:30.840
and while that sounds like a lot of money

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.410
and it is a lot of money,
remember that number one,

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:34.430
they're going to have to live in New York,

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:36.050
which is incredibly
expensive, and number two,

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:38.760
they're probably have to
bill at least 2,400 hours,

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:41.485
which means they're
probably going to be working

00:00:41.485 --> 00:00:42.840
at least 3000 hours a year,

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.380
which means about 60 hours a week.

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:47.010
So yes, these are white collar jobs,

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:49.353
but this is hard work
with very long hours.

